(Bug #54's false-positive guard: a helper that appends to a list it was
 HANDED can widen any list in the program, and the append names the
 parameter rather than the caller's list - so no element-type proof is
 offered anywhere while such a helper exists, and this text read of a
 number list's third element, which the helper made text, still compiles.)

To stash with a list called bag.
    Append "extra" to bag.

a list called counts is [1, 2].
stash with counts.
a text called third is element 3 of counts.
Print third.

(The reads that always matched still answer correctly.)
a number called 'first count' is element 1 of counts.
Print 'first count'.
